  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "Expressed as a fraction in its simplest form, ${log}_{16}⁡(64)$ equals{{field-1}}.",
  "worked_solution": "We use the change of base formula:\n\n$$\n{log}_{a}⁡X=\\frac{{log}_{b}⁡X}{{log}_{b}⁡a}\n$$\n\nIn our case, $a=16$ and $X=64.$ Since both $a$ and $X$ are powers of $2,$ we set $b=2.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{log}_{16}⁡(64) & =\\frac{{log}_{2}⁡(64)}{{log}_{2}⁡(16)} \\\\  & =\\frac{{log}_{2}⁡({2}^{6})}{{log}_{2}⁡({2}^{4})} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
